# Canonical identity for this repository.
#
# Five commits between "Make Rule 09 true" and "Scope 1.1.0" were authored with
# git's fallback identity — a name and email derived from the username and
# hostname of the machine, because neither had been configured. They are the
# same person as every other commit here.
#
# Mapped rather than rewritten, deliberately. All five are published on
# origin/main, and v1.0.1 points at one of them — the commit that published the
# package to npm with provenance. That attestation is immutable and names the
# commit SHA, so rewriting it would leave the published provenance for
# chapbook@1.0.1 pointing at a commit that no longer exists. A cosmetic fix is
# not worth breaking a supply-chain claim the README makes in writing.
#
# git log --use-mailmap, git shortlog and git blame apply this automatically.
Aaron Taylor <hi@aarontaylor.me> Personal <personal@Aarons-MacBook-Pro.local>
